ssignment, I think. Mypy assumes that the second assignment kills the first\n\n```\nx = 65.5  # type: float\nreveal_type(x)  # E: Revealed type is 'builtins.float'\nx = 65\nreveal_type(x)  # E: Revealed type is 'builtins.int'\n```\n\nJust like any other case of compatible assignment. So how is that different from the simpler case\n\n```\nx = 65\nx += 5.0  # E: Unsupported operand types for + (\"int\" and \"float\")\n```\n\nAllowing the latter (inferring float without any other hint) can easily miss real type errors.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/244867350/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"elazarg","id":5108069,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgwNjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5108069?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg","html_url":"https://github.com/elazarg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/244875594","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/2098#issuecomment-244875594","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/2098","id":244875594,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NDg3NTU5NA==","user":{"login":"JdeH","id":1730289,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzAyODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1730289?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH","html_url":"https://github.com/JdeH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-06T07:51:03Z","updated_at":"2016-09-06T07:52:27Z","body":"@elazarg:\n\nIf that's the cause, why then is\n\n```\nweight1 = 65.5\nweight1 = 65\nweight1 = weight1 * 0.5    # Gives no error\n```\n\nconsidered correct?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/244875594/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"JdeH","id":1730289,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzAyODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1730289?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH","html_url":"https://github.com/JdeH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JdeH/subscrip